A frame's time, traced (Kosmos docs/webkit.md, Fast, step 1a; testing.md
18.854). While JetSki's trace is on - the UI process says so, and a web
process hears it in its launch page - the web process times each
display(): rendering (updateRendering and what follows it), the region
made for the picture (ShareableBitmap::create and its handle), and
painting it; and the UI process times the picture taken into its backing
store (BackingStore::incorporateUpdate, a scroll's move of the store's
pixels included). The tallies and the line they make are the port's
(Shared/kosmos/KosmosFrameTimes.cpp); nothing here changes what is drawn.

